# @@PACKAGE@@

An agent harness exported by `architect forge integrate` (architect @@VERSION@@).

Requirements: `architect>=@@VERSION@@` must be installed in the interpreter that runs
this package. Native harnesses import `architect.presets`, and sandbox harnesses
spawn `sys.executable -I -m architect.runtime._sandbox_worker` (`-I` ignores
`PYTHONPATH`), so a vendored copy on the path is not enough.

Usage: the feature is OFF by default. It runs only when the environment variable
`@@FLAG@@` is exactly `1`, after human review. Call `verify()` to re-check the
files, pins and (@@WHERE@@) the license; `run(value, profile=...)` re-verifies at
load and runs through the Architect runtime. The run uses the workspace you pass
as `workspace=...`, else the one `ARCHITECT_WORKSPACE` names, else the profile's.
A profile that names `~/.architect` also reads its stored key or judge code there.

